60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C addresses the privacy gap and the uneven burden. A shared calendar forces accountability, unlike the current first-come, first-served chaos.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Option C offers the structure we lack. A bookable space means we can finally have those difficult conversations without fear of being overheard.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"Option C is a trap. A bookable room just means someone else is always in there, and I am still walking twenty-five minutes for lunch.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option C costs 141,000 yen. That is a significant outlay for a room that still leaks sound. I need to see how that investment stops the monthly bleed before I agree.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Option C offers structure, but a bookable room is not a sanctuary. If the plasterboard remains, we are merely scheduling our exposure. I need to know if the screen truly isolates us.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the 141,000 yen is for the screen, which fixes the leak. @Servas, the screen isolates the room. The calendar ensures fair use, ending the first-come chaos.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, the screen does isolate the room. It creates the privacy we need for honest talk. @May, I hear your frustration, but this is the only option that addresses our isolation.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, privacy is nice, but it doesn't feed me. Option A at least gives me a hot lunch without the twenty-five minute trek.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, the kitchen quote is 96,000 yen, but it ignores the plasterboard. You will still hear every argument. @Ryuji, the screen is the only fix for the leak.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@May, a hot meal is a basic dignity, not a luxury. @Shunichi, the screen is the only true barrier. I lean toward C, but I need assurance the noise stops there.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""May"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, the kitchen does not fix the noise or the unfair clearing. @Shunichi, the screen is the only structural fix. I am leaning toward C for its accountability.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@May, I understand the hunger, but a kitchen invites noise, not connection. @Shunichi, the screen is the only way to protect the fragile trust we are trying to build.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, accountability is a nice word, but it doesn't pay for my time. If C means I'm still walking twenty-five minutes for lunch, I'm out.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, the kitchen is cheaper, but it leaves the plasterboard leak intact. You will still hear every argument. @Ryuji, I am leaning toward C, but only if the screen truly stops the noise.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@May, your time is precious, and I respect that. @Shunichi, the screen is the only true wall. I am leaning toward C, trusting that structure will finally bring peace.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I am voting for C. The shared calendar ends the first-come chaos, and the screen fixes the structural leak. It is the only sustainable choice.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I am voting for C. The screen gives us the privacy to finally speak, and the structure helps us stop being strangers.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,I am voting for A. I need my twenty-five minutes back. A kitchen feeds me and keeps the hours honest.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I am voting for C. The 141,000 yen is the only investment that stops the monthly bleed. The screen fixes the leak; the calendar fixes the chaos.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"I am voting for C. The screen restores the dignity of privacy, and the structure allows our shared space to finally breathe and heal.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
